  "review": {
    "review": "The initiating missed opportunity was in ranged arbitration, not just the final recovery waits. At decision 2970 (log lines 8391–8393), the staff was empty, both throwing clubs were on the visible DM-100's cell, and an identified throwable stone of deep sleep remained carried. The early ranged controller raised NoSafeAction before shared runestone tactics could run; continuation spent the waterskin and then retreated. Offline memory reconstruction matched selected inputs 0–2970; an isolated candidate probe selected the sleep stone, without supplying subsequent observations. This is reconstructed policy state, not recorded memory. Decision 2979's accepted transition (8434) records a hidden explosive trap and HP falling from 33 to 7. Decision 2985's terminal transition (8457) explicitly reports lethal lightning and the Zapped badge; the final killer is not inferred merely from enemy proximity. The clock advanced during recovery. Post-death potion and ring revelations were not treated as prior knowledge. A focused selector correction and new regression are supplied for next-run validation; files is empty because the adapter derives changes. The original selector fails two expected assertions; the candidate passes all nine new tests and the full 1470-test suite, with four skips. This establishes control selection, not a successful throw, safe escape, puzzle completion or survival.",
    "learnings": "Before exhausted ranged arbitration enters best-effort continuation, consider carried, identified point-target control. Preserve clear-shot, eligibility, cooldown, hazard and mandatory-pickup constraints. Selecting sleep is not evidence that it landed or that escape became safe."
